# Template for ~/.zshenv.work  (copy to ~/.zshenv.work and fill in real values).
#
# This file holds location-specific environment and SECRETS. The real file is
# gitignored and must NEVER be committed. ~/.zshrc sources it automatically when
# ~/.zshenv sets LOCATION=work (see .zshenv.example).
#
# The same pattern works for any location: ~/.zshenv.personal, ~/.zshenv.home, …
#
# Put machine-/work-specific exports here. Generic examples (uncomment + edit):
#
#   export AWS_PROFILE="..."
#   export SOME_DB_USER="..."
#   export SOME_DB_PASSWORD="..."
#   export SOME_REGISTRY_TOKEN="..."
#
# Tip: this is just a sourced shell script, so anything valid in zsh works
# (PATH additions, aliases, functions, `eval "$(some-tool init)"`, …).
